    ' THE DRIVE SPAN (task 3595) -- the commanded interval, which ALWAYS runs. Every quantitative
    '  observable this harness had was collected inside bWindowPoint(), and that window only runs once
    '  the point has already reached AT_SPEED; a point that failed before then carried its result token
    '  and nothing else. Those are exactly the boundary points, so the instrument recorded fault and
    '  abort as a BINARY and never measured how far the drive had fallen behind (D2: a discovery
    '  failure must never render as a zero). pollSample() already runs on every path from the command
    '  onward and already reads duty, err, sense, state, fault and cog -- it simply accumulated none of
    '  it. These are that accumulation, opened at the command and closed before the zero command.
    LONG    bSpanOpen                                       ' TRUE between the drive command and the zero command
    LONG    spanStartMs                                     ' getms() at the drive command
    LONG    spanStartTicks                                  ' hall ticks at the drive command
    LONG    spanDriveMs                                     ' the closed span's duration
    LONG    spanDriveTicks                                  ' hall ticks travelled over it, absolute
    LONG    spanDutySum                                     ' duty accumulated over the span
    LONG    spanDutyMax                                     ' the largest duty the servo demanded in it
    LONG    spanSamples                                     ' samples taken in the span

